abstract: >
  GISMO is an open-source MATLAB toolbox for analyzing seismic and infrasound
  waveform data. It provides an object-oriented framework and a set of
  high-level tools for importing, processing, visualizing, and analyzing
  seismo-acoustic data from common observatory and research formats
  (including MiniSEED, SAC, SEISAN, and Antelope/CSS3.0 databases).
  GISMO integrates the MATLAB Waveform Suite, the Correlation Toolbox,
  catalog and detection utilities, and plotting tools for spectrograms,
  RSAM, STA/LTA detections, event rates, and more. It has been used in
  earthquake and volcano seismology, environmental seismology, and education
  at observatories, universities, and research institutions worldwide.

